  "body": "If I set the bit_depth manually to 8, then the script continues for a few more line, until it tries to create a thumbnail:\r\n\r\n```\r\nfound image: 4000x3000 pixels, 8 bits\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"driver.py\", line 18, in <module>\r\n  File \"<string>\", line 449, in <module>\r\n  File \"<string>\", line 445, in main\r\n  File \"<string>\", line 277, in read\r\nAttributeError: module 'pillow_heif' has no attribute 'thumbnail'\r\n```\r\n\r\nLooking at \"requirements.txt\" in commit 9ec6852a43605fe8999c17d73a18c0e0151c575b:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntifffile\r\nnumpy\r\npillow\r\nwebp\r\nOpenEXR\r\npillow_heif\r\n```\r\n\r\nDo this fetch the latest version of the Python modules at build time?\r\n\r\npillow_heif.__version__ is \"0.18.0\", latest version is 0.21.0 according to https://pypi.org/project/pillow-heif/\r\n\r\n\r\n",
